From 86e8995c35695bcad3e95aff880a8045d075c1f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: medvedolog <afadopulo@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:51:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep NAND presets working past T75 and name the port in
 use

Four fixes to the F5 NAND presets, each one found by reading the current
dev branch rather than by a failure in the field.

Runtime gate. `discover()` matched the bootloader version with
`endswith('-t75')`, so the next release would have silently switched the
presets off. It now follows the capability instead: a `tftpput_available`
flag from the firmware when present, otherwise the `-tNN` generation
compared against the release that first shipped `tftpput`. Once UrsusBoot
publishes the flag the inference stops being used.

Transfer port. 1069 was hardcoded in both directions with no fallback, so
a port already taken on the PC ended the preset instead of moving aside.
The port is now chosen once per menu entry, preferring 1069 so firewall
rules stay predictable, and every message names the port actually in use.
The TFTP GET failure also says to check the firewall, which is what it
usually is.

UBI detach. The restore path decided whether to detach from the caller's
status snapshot, taken before discover() ran its own commands. It now
detaches unconditionally through the console session already in hand: a
detach with nothing attached is a no-op, so asking first only added a way
to be wrong. A first attempt to re-read the status over HTTP was dropped
deliberately -- it introduced a second transport dependency immediately
before the destructive phase, which is worse than the staleness it fixed.

Refusal messages. The combined board/geometry/bad-block check reported one
generic sentence for seven different causes. Each now names the field that
disagrees, and a changed bad-block map explains that the archive no longer
describes the unit physically and that the fix is a fresh archive. Both
carry a stable marker -- URSUS_NAND_ARCHIVE_FOREIGN,
URSUS_NAND_BADBLOCK_MAP_CHANGED -- so QA does not depend on NOKIA_LANG.

selftest_ws_console gains the generation gate and the port fallback, and
asserts that UBI is detached before the first erase. It passes in both
locales; the full workflow QA step passes.

